    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0096" n="76" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v2/pg76"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Harvey, United Slates minister, to Mr. Seward,
                        Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1864-01-30"><hi rendition="#italic">January</hi> 30,
                        1864</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Duke de Loulé addressed me a fourth
                    note, (of which a copy in translation is inclosed,) yesterday, on the subject of
                    my recent representation, <pb facs="0097" n="77" xml:id="pg77"/> and from which
                    it appears that the entire authority of every department of His Majesty’s
                    government has now been seriously and energetically invoked to prevent rebel
                    cruisers from arming or equipping in the island ports of this kingdom.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JAMES E. HARVEY.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
